[01:33.72]A no vote does not lower rates immediately.
[01:36.68]The scheduled expiration would still occur in twenty thirty-one.
[01:40.62]Comparing yes and no therefore means comparing future budgets,
[01:44.44]not just this year’s tax bill.
[01:46.80]A voter might prefer protecting existing revenue for education
[01:50.30]and other services,
[01:52.34]with the additional tax concentrated on high earners.
[01:56.16]Making the rates permanent removes repeated expiration deadlines,
[02:00.40]though it does not make the revenue itself predictable.
[02:03.57]You might ask whether a temporary tax should stay
[02:06.27]permanent.
[02:07.49]A skeptical voter could want the state to honor
[02:09.59]the sunset or reduce reliance on a small, volatile
[02:13.39]tax base.
[02:15.03]They may worry about effects on investment or where
